    "narrative": "Our strongest play for today is **Tyler Freeman**, who enters the lineup with a 63.69 efficiency score against Lauer. The matchup against a high-xERA starter (5.28) provides a significant ceiling boost, making him our only \"Strong\" tier starter. Similarly, **Gavin Sheets** sits at 58.96, benefiting from a favorable platoon matchup against Pfaadt and a clean spot in the middle of the order. We are also monitoring **Jung Hoo Lee**; while his 50.12 score is moderate, his 90th-percentile sprint speed makes him a high-leverage target for our scarcity needs, as Gausman\u2019s delivery rhythm creates a opportunistic environment for him to swipe a bag despite the tougher pitching assignment.\n\nOur most difficult decision revolved around the fringe of the rotation, specifically keeping **Geraldo Perdomo** (55.93) active over potential bench options. While **Perdomo** faces a competent Buehler, his position at the top of the lineup remains essential for our daily run production. Conversely, **Masyn Winn** is our lowest-ranked starter at 42.49, hovering near the bench threshold. His struggle against the southpaw Drohan is notable, but he remains active solely due to the lack of viable replacements on our current injury-depleted bench, where stars like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined on the IL.\n\nRisk remains a primary concern with today\u2019s roster, particularly concerning **Bryson Stott**. His 46.34 score is suppressed by a negative platoon split against Cameron and a high-efficiency catcher behind the plate, which creates a significant risk of him being neutralized on the basepaths. We are essentially running **Stott** as a floor play, but if the weather shifts or the matchup becomes more lopsided, he is the first candidate to be capped to preserve our season-long limits. We are currently playing without the upside of **Lawrence Butler**, **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, or **Drew Gilbert**, further thinning our margin for error in these 5x5 categories.",
